-- title:
--   Simple zero of jmath̃-jmath̃^{q^2} at jmath̃=a
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime and let $k$ be a field of characteristic $q$. Inside the field of Laurent series over $k$, write $\tilde\jmath$ for `jqModC k`, the Laurent series $t^{-1}$ times the image under $\mathbb{Z}\to k$ of the power series `jNum` $=E_4^3\cdot$`dedekindEtaUnitInv`, and let `modularFunctionFieldC k 1` be the intermediate field of `LaurentSeries k` over $k$ generated by $\tilde\jmath$ together with its level-one $q$-expansion rescaling `jqNModC k 1`. For an element $a\in k$ satisfying $a^{q^{2}}=a$, consider the place `charLGeomPlaceOfPoint k a` of `modularFunctionFieldC k 1` over $k$, obtained by transporting along the $k$-isomorphism `ratFuncEquivCharLOneC k` from `RatFunc k` the finite place of the rational function field attached to the irreducible polynomial $X-a$; here a place is a valuation subring containing the image of $k$, different from the whole field and a principal ideal ring, and `ord` of an element is minus the logarithm of its adic valuation. The assertion is that the element $\tilde\jmath-\tilde\jmath^{\,q^{2}}$ of `modularFunctionFieldC k 1` has `ord` equal to $1$ at this place, i.e. it vanishes to order exactly one at $\tilde\jmath=a$.
--
--   This is the statement that, in characteristic $q$, the function $\tilde\jmath-\tilde\jmath^{\,q^{2}}$ has a simple zero at each point $a$ of $\mathbb{F}_{q^{2}}$ on the $\tilde\jmath$-line; it supplies a uniformiser along one branch through a node of the special fibre of $X_0(q)$. It is used in the local analysis at such nodes, in particular by [`ModularCurve.NodeLocalized.natCast_le_ord_modularRedLocHom_iff_mem_sup_span_pow`](thm.html#ModularCurve.NodeLocalized.natCast_le_ord_modularRedLocHom_iff_mem_sup_span_pow), [`ModularCurve.NodeLocalized.ord_modularRedLocHom_eq_iff_exists_isUnit`](thm.html#ModularCurve.NodeLocalized.ord_modularRedLocHom_eq_iff_exists_isUnit) and in the construction of inertia-fixed node coordinates at level one.
